      "publication_date": "2023-12-12",
      "abstract": "Breaking with Aristotle\u2019s Physics, Kant effects a theoretical reconception of teleology. It is this paper\u2019s contention that the truth of the Kantian conception of teleology as \u2018a purposiveness of nature in behalf of our faculty for cognizing it\u2019 is not that of being a solution to Hume\u2019s problem of induction or the condition for the possibility of subjective cognition of the empirical, but that it is a theoretical means of the subjective domination over the objective. A materialist reading of Hegel\u2019s criticism of Kant\u2019s antinomy of teleological judgment in the Science of Logic is then proposed. Finally, the non-teleological nature of capital is demonstrated.",
